[Music]  I'm really grateful to be here in Berlin  because the city gave me the chance to  realize my own projects and to have a  vision and maybe also realize something  that was not planned before so that's  why I'm here at the restaurant  [Music]  Federico testa comes from Bologna where  he was born in 1982 his father ran a  popular restaurant there for 35 years  when Federico came to Berlin his career  in the catering industry began rather by  chance in a restaurant called tabatha  because as a trained musician and  photographer  he actually had very different plans I  [Music]  came in Berlin in 2008 because I wanted  to play music with a friend of mine and  then things went completely different as  we planned and started to work as a  photographer and Francisca my friend a  chef and then together we started to  cook for friends and it became a  restaurant  after de Buffy closed Federico opened  his own restaurant Bosco in 2014 in  Berlin's hip courts back district he  lives nearby one of more than 4,000  Italians living in Kreuzberg  [Music]  before opening for business Federico  spent five months renovating the place  he did a lot of work himself his idea  was to create a modern and welcoming  atmosphere  [Music]  eating in Italy is a very important role  because around the table big decision  I've made and you can talk about every  topic on the table with a nice glass of  wine that makes everything softer and of  course also good food makes it  everything smooth the menu changes  regularly according to the season  Federico wants his guests to enjoy  traditional Italian food the kind he  enjoyed as a child  [Music]  tortelloni with ragout ricotta cheese  and spinach combines modern with  traditional cuisine the recipe for the  ragu prepared with vegetables and ground  beef comes from Bologna there it's  traditionally eaten with pasta total Oni  also come from northern Italy there is  similar to totally knee but are much  larger  [Music]  normally tortelloni are filled with  vegetables and served with the ragu  sauce  [Music]  the dish we presented today is a total  only with ragout filled with ricotta and  peanuts which is the rid original and we  made it upside down so fit with ragout  and with the cream of ricotta spinach  and to me reminds me really of my  Sundays and my Sundays at my grandma  because that was what she was always  cooking for me like fresh pasta is a  very simple recipe but it's well made  it's like heaven to begin with Federico  worked in the kitchen too but now he  devotes all of his time to being out  front catering to his customers  [Music]  Audio demo kuchi not over boy tortelloni  rapini ragù alla Bolognese Cory Cortez  Panaji bon appetito

